 "notes": "Single map sheet read from OCR (page 1). Map symbols are garbled or not clearly tied to a unit in the OCR text ('SHme', '[ QHiw', 'QPldm') and were not recorded. The Water unit was not recorded. The map-symbol explanation (contact) was not recorded: legend-only features are not values. Two thicknesses printed as '| to N feet' are read as 1, flagged inferred and sent to review. Georgia portions of the quadrangle are not mapped.\nSUBSURFACE: Ladson Formation margin elevations (above 35 ft seaward where overlapped by the Ten Mile Hill beds, below 57 ft landward against the Penholoway Formation; page 1). No drill holes, cross sections or structure contours appear in the OCR text. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum; contour interval 10 feet on the 1978 base map; the vertical datum is not stated (page 1).\nRe-read of page 1 for subsurface fields (single OCR map sheet; most of the quadrangle is the unmapped Georgia area). Units as before; map symbols read from the legend boxes on a page-image tile. Two thicknesses printed '| to N feet' read as 1 (inferred). Ladson Formation margin elevations (above 35 ft seaward, below 57 ft landward) recorded as contacts and as stated unit tops at those margins (boundary inferred; no vertical datum printed). Whole-page image checked: no drill holes, cross sections or structure contours. Water unit, unmapped Georgia area and legend-only contact not recorded.",
